  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): オオオニバス",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AA%E3%83%8B%E3%83%90%E3%82%B9",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 111299319,
      "text": "オオオニバス は、スイレン科オオオニバス属に属する水生植物の1種である。直径2メートル (m) 以上になる巨大な浮水葉を水面に浮かべることで知られている（図1）。南米のアマゾン川流域に生育し、植物園などで栽培されることもある。属名の Victoria はイギリスのビクトリア女王に、種小名の amazonica はその生育地にちなんで命名された。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Victoria amazonica",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_amazonica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1374550559,
      "text": "Victoria amazonica is a species of flowering plant, the second largest in the water lily family Nymphaeaceae. It is called Vitória-Régia or Iaupê-Jaçanã in Brazil and Atun Sisac in Inca (Quechua). Its native region is tropical South America, specifically Guyana and the Amazon Basin."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Victoria amazonica",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_amazonica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 168196468,
      "text": "Victoria amazonica, nombre común Victoria regia, es un nenúfar nativo de las aguas poco profundas de la cuenca del Amazonas."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Victoria amazonica",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_amazonica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 238550907,
      "text": "Victoria amazonica, la Victoria d'Amazonie ou Nénuphar géant, est une espèce de plantes à fleurs de la famille des Nymphaeaceae."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Victoria amazonica",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_amazonica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 72084174,
      "text": "A vitória-régina ou victória-régia é uma planta aquática da família das Nymphaeaceae, típica da região amazônica."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Teratai raksasa",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teratai_raksasa",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 30063115,
      "text": "Victoria amazonica juga disebut Victoria regia adalah spesies tumbuhan berbunga terbesar kedua dalam keluarga teratai Nymphaeaceae. Itu disebut Uape Jacana di Brasil dan nama Inca (Quechua) adalah Atun Sisac. Daerah asalnya adalah Amerika Selatan tropis, khususnya Guyana dan Lembah Amazon."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Victoria amazonica § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victoria_amazonica#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1374550559,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "V. amazonica is cultivated in botanical gardens worldwide, requiring warm water temperatures of 29–32°C (85–90°F) for optimal growth; mature plants tolerate slightly cooler conditions (24–27°C or 75–80°F). Propagation is primarily by seed, which should be stored submerged in water and scarified to accelerate germination. Rhizome division is also possible during the growing season. In temperate regions, it is grown as an annual in containers with organically rich loam substrate in still water 1–3 m deep.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
